  "ai-20261016-1757-lf01": {
   "id": "ai-20261016-1757-lf01",
   "pack": "ai-2026-10-16-1757-longform",
   "stem": "A financial services company is migrating a legacy database application to AWS. The software vendor licenses the product per physical socket and core under a bring-your-own-license model, and auditors require proof that each licensed instance stays on the same physical server over time. The operations team also needs visibility into the physical sockets and cores in use. The security team requires that no other customer's workloads share the underlying hardware. Which solution will meet these requirements?",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "text": "Launch the instances as Dedicated Instances in a dedicated-tenancy VPC and report the physical core count from instance metadata"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "text": "Launch Spot Instances in a cluster placement group and tag each instance with its license details to document placement over time"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "text": "Launch On-Demand Instances with default tenancy in a partition placement group and map each partition to a licensed server"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "text": "Allocate Dedicated Hosts, launch the instances onto them with host affinity set to Host, and track sockets and cores per host"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "D"
   ],
   "explanation": "Dedicated Hosts expose the physical sockets and cores, and host affinity set to Host keeps an instance on the same physical server after stop/start, which is what a per-socket BYOL audit needs.\n- Dedicated Instances: single-tenant hardware, but no host affinity and no visibility into sockets or cores.\n- Spot Instances in a cluster placement group: placement groups control network locality, not which physical host is used, and Spot can be reclaimed.\n- Partition placement group on default tenancy: partitions isolate failure domains on shared hardware and give no socket or core visibility.\n> 🇻🇳 BYOL theo socket/core + cùng máy vật lý → Dedicated Hosts với host affinity = Host.",
   "domain": "secure",
   "topic": "compute",
   "services": [
    "EC2"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "dedicated-hosts",
    "host-affinity"
   ],
   "difficulty": "hard",
